  <data name="Privacy_Intro" xml:space="preserve"><value>A short summary of the data CarRental keeps and how the AI assistant works.</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_DataTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Account and rentals</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_DataText" xml:space="preserve"><value>When you register we store your first name, last name and e-mail. For every rental we store the car, dates, total, status and your notes. This data is needed to process bookings; it is visible to you and to the service administrator.</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_ChatTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Chat history</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_ChatText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Chat messages and the assistant's replies are stored in the database together with the chat session. If you are signed in, the session belongs to your account and is never shown to other users. The session id is kept in your browser; the New chat button starts a new conversation.</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_AiTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Processing by language models</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_AiText" xml:space="preserve"><value>To reply, the assistant sends your messages and the context it needs (for example, cars it found and fragments of the rental rules) to an external language model provider, Google Gemini or Groq. Do not write passwords, card numbers, passport data or other sensitive information in the chat.</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_BookingTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Bookings only with your confirmation</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_BookingText" xml:space="preserve"><value>The assistant can only prepare a booking draft. A rental is created only after you press Confirm; the assistant cannot confirm bookings, take payments or change prices.</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_CookiesTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Cookies</value></data>
  <data name="Privacy_CookiesText" xml:space="preserve"><value>The site uses only necessary cookies: for signing in, remembering your language and protecting forms against request forgery (antiforgery). There are no advertising or third-party analytics cookies.</value></data>
